msgstr "Kipi"

#. Tag: title
#: slideshow.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Advanced Slide Show"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this Kipi-plugin you create a perfect slide show with just three mouse "
"clicks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: slideshow.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Settings Dialog"
msgstr "Dijalog postavki"

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When opening the plugin from the host application, the <guilabel>Advanced "
"Slide Show</guilabel> window will appear asking questions as to how you want "
"to stage your slideshow. You can choose between the selected images or all "
"images in the same album."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Use OpenGL Slideshow Transitions</guilabel> checkbox enables "
"very smooth image transitions using the OpenGL display mode. Be sure you "
"have OpenGL enabled on your graphics card, since otherwise the slideshow "
"will be very slow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Print Filename</guilabel> checkbox enables displaying the "
"image filename in the lower left corner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Loop</guilabel> checkbox will enable running the whole show in "
"an endless loop (until manually stopped with <keycombo>&Esc;</keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Shuffle Image</guilabel> checkbox will enable displaying the "
"images randomly (not using the current images collection order)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Delay Between Images</guilabel> may be set in millisecond "
"steps. 1500 milliseconds correspond to 1.5 seconds and is a good default "
"value. The best timing depends also a bit on your computer power and the "
"transition effect. Try it out before you show it to your friends!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are more than a dozen <guilabel>Transition Effects</guilabel> "
"available to choose from. The <guilabel>Random</guilabel> selection will "
"change the transition effect with every image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: slideshow.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Slideshow Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: slideshow.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Slide Show in Action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During the slideshow, you can access a toolbar on the upper left screen "
"corner. Move the mouse cursor to the top left of the screen to access it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this tool bar, you can drive the progress of the slideshow. You can "
"pause or play the slideshow, go back to the preview image, go to the next "
"image, and stop the slideshow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: slideshow.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the lower left screen corner you can see the current image file name, the "
"current image ID, and the total number of images included in the slideshow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: slideshow.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Advanced Slideshow Plugin in Action"
msgstr ""
